  "name": "Question 11",
  "problem": "If $U={0,1,2,\u2026,50}$ is the universal set and $X={40,41,42,\u202650}$ then the complement of $X$ is",
  "worked_solution": "The complement of $X,$ denoted $\\overset{\u2015}{X},$ consists of every element in the universal set $U$ that is not in the set $X.$\n\nThe universal set $U$ consists of the integers $0$ through $50,$ while the set $X$ consists of the integers $40$ through $50.$\n\nSo, the only elements of $U$ that are not in $A$ are the integers $0$ through $39.$\n\nTherefore, the complement of $X$ is\n\n$$\n\\overset{\u2015}{X}={0,1,2,\u2026,39}.\n$$",
